# Environment for submit_field_spinup.sh / Cluster_Field_Spinup_Task: the
# Hamden (145 Blue Trail, CT) field spin-up.  Copy to field_spinup_hamden.env,
# set the paths and submit:  bash submit_field_spinup.sh field_spinup_hamden.env
# Paths are POSIX paths on the cluster.
#
# Grid: 5 m squares, the coarsest width at which the parcel's terrain
# statistics have converged, each kept when more than half of it lies in the
# parcel, on the lattice that minimises the misrepresented area: 936 cells,
# 2.3 % of the parcel misrepresented (TC_CELL_M, TC_MIN_COVERAGE below; the
# per-cell file is tied to this grid).
# The site borrows the workbook's case-5 rows and replaces what differs:
#   TC_MOD_COLUMNS_FILE  location, the Hamden vegetation file (trees over
#                        grass mown on 1 September), NOAA daily CO2, CT15 wet
#                        and TDep dry deposition by event (N, K, Ca, Mg, and
#                        the ERW chemistry's Na and SO4 + Cl), CT15's rain
#                        record for the ERW's rain pH, the NLDAS-2 forcing
#                        and the windows; the soil column stays the base
#                        file's default (20 layers to 5 m, free drainage);
#   TC_ERW_COLUMNS_FILE  no rock; every cell's base saturation emerges from
#                        the spin-up (spinup_equilibrium) unless the per-cell
#                        file gives it a measured one; bulk pH by a 1:1
#                        water extract; Na and SO4 + Cl from deposition
#                        alone (keyword_add 0).
# Each cell's soil (Cheshire texture; its map unit's pH and OM; the
# representative effective CEC) and land cover (NLCD
# 2020 shares) come from TC_AGRONOMIC_FILE (Run_Hamden_Field_Inputs).  The
# simulation is the whole field: every cell, no buffer region.
#
# Inputs: the NLDAS-2 forcing Data_Hamden.mat (v2/T&C_Code/Inputs, 2014-12-30
# to 2026-09-30 local) and the parcel's DEM window,
# USGS_1M_18_x67y459_CT_Statewide_C16_parcel_window.tif, in
# v2/Spatial inputs/Hamden Blue Trail/DEM (not versioned in git: upload it
# with the code).
#
# Dates: the ring is 2015-2018 (four complete years); 2019 runs once as the
# handoff extension and the state hands off at 2020-01-01 00:00, the first
# hour of the simulation and validation runs, 2020-01-01 to 2026-09-29
# (transient_start, transient_end and NumberOfDays are in the MOD columns
# file; the TC_TRANSIENT_* variables below take precedence).
#
# Cost (flux_tracking): one class seed (every cell shares texture and
# vegetation), a cold plot-scale spin-up of several hours; the 2-D tracking
# run, five segments (four ring years and the extension) of about a day
# each; 94 replays of a few hours each in parallel; 842 forest
# reconstructions of minutes each.  A job near its 1-day limit requeues
# itself and resumes its checkpoints (requeue_on_timeout.sh), so the chain
# runs to the end unattended.
#
# Warm start, once the site observations are in the per-cell file (the
# measured_* columns, or a new representative set): set TC_WARM_START_STATES
# to this run's CellBGStates.mat (copy it out of scratch first), give a new
# TC_OUTPUT_DIR and submit again.  No class seed is spun up; the tracking
# starts from every cell's converged state; each replay runs Phase 3 only (a
# Control 2 cell re-converged in 24 coupled years after a pH, CEC and base
# saturation change, against 306 from cold); the exchanger is seeded from
# the new inputs at the handoff.

TC_ROOT=$HOME/project_pi_<netid>/TC-SMEW-N          # folder holding v2
TC_SHAPEFILE="$TC_ROOT/v2/Spatial inputs/Hamden Blue Trail/Hamden_Blue_Trail_Parcel.shp"
TC_DEM="$TC_ROOT/v2/Spatial inputs/Hamden Blue Trail/DEM"
TC_AGRONOMIC_FILE="$TC_ROOT/v2/T&C_Code/Inputs/Field_Spinup/Hamden/Cell_Agronomic_Hamden_Blue_Trail_Parcel_polygon_01.csv"
TC_MOD_COLUMNS_FILE="$TC_ROOT/v2/T&C_Code/Inputs/Field_Spinup/Hamden/Hamden_MOD_columns.csv"
TC_ERW_COLUMNS_FILE="$TC_ROOT/v2/T&C_Code/Inputs/Field_Spinup/Hamden/Hamden_ERW_columns.csv"
TC_OUTPUT_DIR=$HOME/scratch_pi_<netid>/TC-SMEW-N/Hamden_flux   # scratch is purged after 30 days: copy results out
# TC_WARM_START_STATES=$HOME/project_pi_<netid>/TC-SMEW-N/runs/Hamden_flux/CellBGStates.mat

TC_METHOD=flux_tracking     # flux_tracking (Lian et al. 2025) | per_cell (1-D reference)
TC_POLYGON=1
TC_CELL_M=5
TC_MIN_COVERAGE=majority
TC_SUBSAMPLE=0.10
TC_TRACK_JOBS=8
TC_CASE=5
# TC_MAX_REQUEUES=10        # requeues per job when its time limit nears (requeue_on_timeout.sh)

# The windows are in TC_MOD_COLUMNS_FILE; set these only to override them.
# TC_TRANSIENT_START=2020-01-01
# TC_TRANSIENT_END=2026-09-29

TC_VALIDATE=0
